Feature: Fix Wayland content offset ("phantom shadow") after window is hidden and re-shown, e.g. minimise to tray (issues #399, follow-up to #563).

When a window is re-mapped after being hidden, moz_container_wayland_map_event()
re-creates the content wl_subsurface at position (0,0), and no size-allocate
with a changed allocation follows to correct it via MoveLocked() when the
geometry is unchanged. The painted content then appears shifted by the CSD
decoration offset while hit-testing stays correct. Reuse the container's
current allocation as the initial subsurface position on re-map; a later
size-allocate corrects it if it is stale. A (0,0) allocation keeps the old
behaviour, so first map and non-CSD windows are unaffected.

diff --git a/widget/gtk/MozContainerWayland.cpp b/widget/gtk/MozContainerWayland.cpp
--- a/widget/gtk/MozContainerWayland.cpp
+++ b/widget/gtk/MozContainerWayland.cpp
@@ -142,9 +142,19 @@ gboolean moz_container_wayland_map_event
       MOZ_WL_CONTAINER(container)->before_first_size_alloc) {
     return false;
   }
 
-  return moz_container_wayland_ensure_surface(container);
+  // On re-map (e.g. after minimise to tray) the container still carries its
+  // allocation, which for CSD windows is offset by the decoration margin
+  // inside the toplevel. Use it as the initial subsurface position so the
+  // re-created surface does not stick at (0,0) when no size-allocate with
+  // changed geometry follows (issue #399 phantom shadow).
+  GtkAllocation allocation;
+  gtk_widget_get_allocation(widget, &allocation);
+  DesktopIntPoint allocPos(allocation.x, allocation.y);
+  DesktopIntPoint* pos =
+      (allocation.x != 0 || allocation.y != 0) ? &allocPos : nullptr;
+  return moz_container_wayland_ensure_surface(container, pos);
 }
 
 void moz_container_wayland_size_allocate(GtkWidget* widget,
                                          GtkAllocation* allocation) {
